{
  "$comment": "v1.9 (D-066) the veld soundscape (Tech §7.1, art bible §10.2): one-shot calls of each area's birds, insects and weather over its ambience bed, scheduled on sim time by src/game/audio/soundscape.ts (presentation only: no sim state, no replay). Per area, each entry plays `call` about perMinute times a minute (× the time-of-day factor of its `profile` for the hunt's light, ± jitter), at levelDb plus its distance's level and low-pass (far = quieter and muffled), panned to a random screen x. weight orders calls due at the same moment (the higher one gets the voice). At most maxVoices soundscape voices at once and never fewer than reserveVoices of the 16 left free for the game; minGapMs between any two call starts. Lights: the profiles give every layout light a factor; a bonus map's haze adds its hazeDb (further back sounds further away); a special day's light (or none) falls back to the map's own layout light, else defaultLight. Calls that `warns` a penalty creature (hadeda, fish eagle, kwêvoël) are far only, and none plays from quietBeforeEventMs before that creature's world event until quietAfterEventMs after it has left the screen, so the event's own call stays the player's warning. The title plays the area on screen at titleRateMul. Sounds are sfx/amb_* keys (interim synths in tools/audio/soundscape.ts, lazy group `soundscape`).",
